As CADO, I am responsible for leading the school's overall data strategy, providing leadership and strategic direction over all data administration efforts and building analytics capacity to drive decisions with data that are crucial to the success and reputation to NYU Stern as a top ranked business school.  

Specific Responsibilities Include:
• Creating and leading the school's "Center for Excellence" in business analytics, engaging with key stake holders at the school to create a cross-functional competency area that provides leadership, best practices, support, and training around analytics;
• Developing and enhancing the school's business intelligence and reporting capabilities to accelerate and improve decision making;
• Responsible for school wide data management overseeing the entire the school’s data pipeline from data collection to data analysis by serving as the nexus between strategic decision making and information technology and data resources.  Working in close collaboration with key data owners and institutional data stewards to establish an enterprise data road map and data management process that enables information sharing, collaboration, compliance and security in support of the School’s data Strategy.  
• Responsible for re-building the school’s entire data ecosystem with a comprehensive and systematic approach to data architecture (Stern 360) that ensures consistent use and reuse of data, enabling an enterprise to link all of its critical data to a common point of reference; and improves data quality, while streamlining data sharing across personnel and departments to provide self service and on-demand analytics.

